<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Yusuf Yaqub ibn Abd al-Haqq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1212–1286</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Yusuf Yaqub ibn Abd al-Haqq was sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinid dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> from 1258 to 1286. In 1269 he captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a>, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> rule, and in 1276 he founded the royal city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fes-el-jdid">Fes el-Jdid</a> beside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a>. He crossed several times to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> to support the Nasrids of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-yusuf-yaqub-ibn-abd-al-haqq.jpg" alt="Abu Yusuf Yaqub ibn Abd al-Haqq" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alfonso X (Life time: 1221-1284) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MoorandChristianBattle.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
